[style name="style"]
do GameManager.set_dialogue_on(true)
join adam left [animation="Slide From Left"]
Not_Name: Hello. Are you new here?
join main_character right [animation="Slide From Right" mirrored="true"]
main_character: Uh, yeah. Who are you?
adam: Call me Adam. Glad to meet a new face.
adam: How are you?
main_character: (I should mind my words...)
- print("Hello world")
	adam: What?
	main_character: Sorry, a joke.
	adam: Okay...
	leave adam [animation="Slide To Left" wait="true"]
	update main_character center
	main_character: (I messed that one up...)
	leave main_character [animation="Slide To Right"]
	do GameManager.subtract_wave(1)
- Nice, what about you?
	adam: Well, we're both kinda newbies here. So here's a piece of advice\: take it in your own rhythm and you'll be fine.
	adam: If you feel overwhelmed there's always the option to chill out from time to time.
	adam: It's easy to say, of course, but it's just as easy to forget.
	if {Dictionary.Chill} == false:
		main_character: Chill?
		adam: You know, listening to your body and giving importance only to the things that matter.
		adam: Sheesh. Never been relaxed in your life or anything?
		main_character: (So chill means... relaxed. Got it.)
		do GameManager.set_dialogue_wave(true)
		set {Dictionary.Chill} = true
	main_character: Thank you for the advice.
	adam: No problem. See ya.
	leave adam [animation="Slide To Left" wait="true"]
	update main_character center
	main_character: (My own rhythm, hm?)
	main_character: (But I have a task to fulfill and the day is still progressing...)
	leave main_character [animation="Slide To Right" wait="true"]
	do GameManager.add_wave()
do GameManager.set_dialogue_on(false)